{"title":"2021 WSMO Speed Round Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nBobby is going to throw 20 darts at the dartboard shown below. It is formed by 4 concentric circles, with radii of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/97827a34a0f6699ae2b5fd23665cc8eecd056286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,3,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, with the largest circle being inscribed in a square. Each point on the dartboard has an equally likely chance of being hit by a dart, and Bobby is guaranteed to hit the dartboard. Each region is labeled with its point value (the number of points Bobby will get if he hits that region). The expected number of points Bobby will get after throwing the 20 darts can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43e8a8e8711c11f71a1c61eb0f57063b4cc4c2b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. </p><center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa99ca5c6ecf34b940029025c5aee1edd26e0b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(5cm);  filldraw(shift(-7,-7)*((0,0)--(14,0)--(14,14)--(0,14)--cycle),gray);  filldraw(circle((0,0),7),white); filldraw(circle((0,0),5),white); filldraw(circle((0,0),3),white); filldraw(circle((0,0),1),white);  label(&quot;$70$&quot;,(0,0)); label(&quot;$-28$&quot;,(0,2)); label(&quot;$49$&quot;,(0,4)); label(&quot;$-21$&quot;,(0,6)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;,(-6,6)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;,(6,6)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;,(-6,-6)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;,(6,-6)); [/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"238\" /> </center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Speed_Round_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability of a dart getting 70 points is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/44432432e08dd4b79941ac512309ccb17b7927dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{196}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"34\" />, the probability of a dart getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793d5dcb73a0a81d0d7ab8b71040d5f0308e2c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-28$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> points is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/88021ac37144baa167ea1a9a487e17a925e7bb95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8\\pi}{196}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />, the probability of a dart getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> points is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/4596450848204dd7a8a9284f2133ee74169d3e1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16\\pi}{196}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"35\" height=\"38\" />, and the probability of a dart getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/481aa8fd3205ddca64b0c5f46dab544c8a74aa36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> points is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f70ef89b1fb759268b4582828a910dd1fce5c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{24\\pi}{196}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"35\" height=\"38\" />. This means that on a random throw, the expected number of points Bobby gets is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b719ac9eb8d1debe8cd7deec962066f55cc18f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[70 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{196} - 28 \\cdot \\frac{8\\pi}{196} + 49 \\cdot \\frac{16\\pi}{196} - 21 \\cdot \\frac{24\\pi}{196} = \\frac{9}{14}\\pi.\\]\" width=\"380\" height=\"37\" /> After 20 throws, Bobby is expected to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c29f4bd3386c6ed084da713c1aebf7f9bf9ab83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20\\cdot\\frac{9}{14}\\pi=\\frac{90}{7}\\pi\\implies90+7=\\boxed{97}.\\]\" width=\"277\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018020427\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 67/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3401/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22391:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018020427 and revision id 274582. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}